# Conductive Machete: "When this Equipment enters, manifest dread, then attach this Equipment to that creature." (CR 701.62a,
# 400.7). On turn 3 Bot1 casts it with Black Lotus and Mox Ruby; with its trigger on the stack Bot2 Disenchants it. The trigger
# still resolves: Bot1 looks at Llanowar Elves and Lightning Bolt, manifests the Elves (a face-down 2/2) and bins the Bolt, but
# the Machete in the graveyard is a new object and attaches to nothing - the face-down creature stays a plain 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Conductive Machete
Plains x5
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Disenchant
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Conductive Machete.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Conductive Machete)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Conductive Machete; Black Lotus
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Llanowar Elves | Lightning Bolt)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Conductive Machete; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDownName = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield..Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield..Toughness = 2
